  "body": "Backpressured SENDACKs currently appear as `unknown` in Prometheus, and an incomplete delivery warning cannot be joined to its committed message. Preserve the existing `system_busy` reason through both metric classifiers and include the exact unsigned message ID and sequence in the existing terminal observation and failure warning.\n\nThe change adds two scalar observation fields and one fixed metric reason. Delivery, wire responses, permission checks, queues, timeouts, retries, and successful-plan logging retain their existing behavior. This supplies evidence for the ongoing v3 RC diagnosis; it does not resolve the original cloud expiry or establish release readiness.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Retained assertion/compile REDs before the corresponding production changes, including the intermediate app-only classifier failure and one explicitly corrected test-fixture assumption.\n- Four complete related unit packages: 671 top-level tests, 1,019 passing events, no failures or skips. Covers terminal outcomes, exact uint64 values above MaxInt64, metric normalization, existing labels, and successful-plan silence.\n- `git diff --check` passed. Independent Standards and Spec review and the first exact-source Linux CI are recorded separately before merge.\n",
